I was talking to someone about the castle, namely how a middle-
game character might get themselves out of the castle if they
came at it from the right/back. The moat does not block
the back door, but the need for levitation may be greater
because of the trap doors. Sure, you have scrolls of earth
from Sokoban, but plugging up the trap doors with boulders
might not be what you want to do, since they're the easiest
way to the valley, and you can't recreate them by digging
down.

He then asked why you still couldn't dig down--the floor
is too hard to dig into, but the boulders you used the fill
the pits aren't.  Not until they land in the holes, it seems.

I'm generally fine with the amusing justifications of boulder
behavior but this one seems to take a stretch...

